ach to understanding participation in government nutrition programs#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#A machine learning (ML) approach to understanding participation in government nutrition programs#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/C7TNKHGT","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/U8T6JZKW?page=2&annotation=LLFKNC9G","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/U8T6JZKW?page=2&annotation=WP4DYDK7","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/U8T6JZKW?page=2&annotation=WSU2YVZQ","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 4","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/U8T6JZKW?page=4&annotation=C7RRIT8I","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"A machine learning (ML) approach to understanding participation in government nutrition programs","Authors":"Stacey R. Finkelstein, Rohini Daraboina, Andrea Leschewski, Semhar Michael","Year":2024,"DOI":"10.1016/j.copsyc.2024.101830","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"To begin to address questions of food-decision making, incorporating family and cultural dynamics, and the potential for health impacts, we describe a dynamic approach using MLto predict a specific aspect of participation, attrition, in a government sponsored nutrition education program (EFNEP). Understanding attrition impacts our ability to evaluate the impact of programming on diet quality, food security, physical activity, food safety skills, and food resource management. From a policy perspective, EFNEP participation results in improved modifiable risk factors of chronic disease and there are significant budgetary implications to understanding program attrition and efficacy [15].The Expanded Food and Nutrition Education Program (EFNEP) is the nation’s oldest nutrition education program for families with low-income2023. The program emphasizes behavioral change to improve participant’s dietary quality, food security, physical activity, food resource management, and food safety skills","Findings":"","Conclusions":"Collectively, ML methods, validated with qualitative and survey data, can offer a multitude of benefits, including educating program participants, informing program improvements, and implementing effective modifications.  This approach fosters the development of a robust and sophisticated model that identifies the dynamic factors predicting dropout at each stage of the prog","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"13xs8on","at":1769797077804}},"smart_blocks:Augmented Dietitian Okunmuşlar/A machine learning (ML) approach to understanding participation in government nutrition programs.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.04122962,-0.0023542,0.02363403,-0.0332803,-0.00720069,0.0440984,-0.00283511,0.06591722,-0.02146951,0.01156171,0.01230214,-0.09574324,0.02960603,-0.01471727,0.0698958,-0.03191038,-0.00450466,0.04375377,-0.03248721,0.01814517,0.04533797,-0.03931782,-0.00976601,-0.02076359,0.07807934,0.03427337,-0.04286321,-0.05087984,-0.07042821,-0.21902925,0.04710998,-0.0377143,0.08310859,-0.01758448,-0.06392342,0.0232636,0.02034026,0.03048692,-0.01559415,0.01206419,0.05427816,-0.00335446,0.03485275,-0.04913437,-0.0005749,-0.07887068,-0.00583511,-0.03765295,-0.09160691,-0.02684191,-0.04579118,-0.06139724,0.0258981,0.05804629,0.06389461,0.0729721,0.00875712,0.01277033,0.04476931,0.10898226,0.00526954,0.07704945,-0.23684718,0.0994146,0.02787777,0.08111715,-0.06252632,0.01877414,0.02728475,-0.05533194,-0.07238472,0.03801204,0.01549617,0.04766109,-0.0263636,0.03368093,0.0643687,-0.03865347,-0.01537584,-0.02623534,0.01509891,0.08166037,-0.01552384,-0.01232418,-0.02987379,-0.04448395,-0.01291821,-0.05547546,0.05318959,-0.03023964,-0.0404728,-0.01273418,0.00675272,-0.000677